  "legacy_forever": {
    "comment": "Where the oldest admitted kernel (stock 2.6.14, read with 2.6.35) turns a long finite wait into forever. long_max is MAX_SCHEDULE_TIMEOUT on a 32-bit ABI; hz_max is the largest HZ these platforms offer; the two ceilings are derived from them by the kernel's own tests (poll: timeout < long_max / hz; sock_set_timeout: tv_sec < long_max / hz - 1). max_datagram is the 16-bit IPv6 payload length minus the 8-byte UDP header.",
